    "class": 8,
    "subject": "science",
    "chapter_number": 1,
    "chapter_name": "crop production and management",
    "question_type": "conceptual",
    "question_text": "Explain how fertilisers are different from manure.",
    "question_latex": null,
    "mcq_options": [],
    "correct_option": null,
    "question_image": {
      "present": false,
      "description": null,
      "cloudinary_url": null,
      "latex_extracted": null,
      "source_page_number": null,
      "source_image_index": null,
      "ownership": "unknown"
    },
    "parts": [],
    "answer_text": "Fertilisers are commercially available plant nutrients, while manure is a natural substance prepared by the decomposition of animal excreta and plant wastes. Manure contains a large quantity of organic materials and very little amount of plant nutrients, whereas fertilisers can be organic or inorganic and ensure healthy growth by providing essential nutrients. The addition of fertilisers requires special guidelines, while manure does not. Fertilisers do not provide humus to the soil, while manure does and helps in recycling farm waste.",
    "answer_latex": null,
    "steps": [],
    "final_answer": "Thus, fertilisers and manure differ significantly in their composition and effects on soil.",
    "answer_image": {
      "present": false,
      "description": null,
      "cloudinary_url": null,
      "latex_extracted": null,
      "source_page_number": null,
      "source_image_index": null,
      "ownership": "unknown"
    },
