    "question_image": {
      "present": false,
      "description": null,
      "cloudinary_url": null,
      "latex_extracted": null,
      "source_page_number": null,
      "source_image_index": null,
      "ownership": "unknown"
    },
    "parts": [],
    "answer_text": "Irrigation is the process by which water is supplied to crops at different intervals. Two methods of irrigation that conserve water are: (a) Sprinkler system: This system is useful on uneven land, where water supply is limited. Water is supplied through pipes to central locations in the field and sprinkled on crops under high pressure. (b) Drip system: This method delivers water directly to the roots of plants, minimizing evaporation and runoff.",
    "answer_latex": null,
    "steps": [],
    "final_answer": "Both methods effectively conserve water while ensuring crops receive adequate moisture.",
