    "question_type": "conceptual",
    "question_text": "If wheat is sown in the kharif season, what would happen? Discuss.",
    "question_latex": null,
    "mcq_options": [],
    "correct_option": null,
    "question_image": {
      "present": false,
      "description": null,
      "cloudinary_url": null,
      "latex_extracted": null,
      "source_page_number": null,
      "source_image_index": null,
      "ownership": "unknown"
    },
    "parts": [],
    "answer_text": "If wheat is sown in the kharif season (from June to October), then the whole crop might get destroyed because of many factors such as lack of optimum temperature, adaptability, availability of pests, etc. Kharif season includes the rainy season, which is not favourable for the growth of wheat crop. Therefore, wheat crop should not be sown during this season.",
    "answer_latex": null,
    "steps": [],
    "final_answer": "Therefore, wheat crop should not be sown during the kharif season.",
    "answer_image": {
      "present": false,
